WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.165
Your class is going to build one fingerboard skate park. Each team of three designs up to four sections.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.032
Ramps, ledges, rails, stairs: whatever you dream up.

00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:17.118
Every section uses the same class connector and clearance, so they all snap together.

00:00:17.118 --> 00:00:22.097
Each section must fit within one hundred eighty millimeters, at real fingerboard scale.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.398
In Week 17, you plan and design. Your park plan is due Thursday, May thirteenth.

00:00:29.398 --> 00:00:34.761
In Week 18, you finish your models and check them. Print files are due May twentieth.

00:00:34.761 --> 00:00:39.741
In Week 19, licensed students print, and you fit, ride-test, and revise.

00:00:39.741 --> 00:00:43.120
In Week 20, you assemble the whole park and show it off.

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:54.740
Before you submit print files, run the pre-flight check. Fits the plate. Uses the standard. Prints flat. Nothing too thin. Millimeters. Named right.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.853
Print files are due May twentieth. Submit any section that passes early, so there's time to print before school ends.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:09.472
When sections come back, fit them together and save a named version in Onshape for each revision.

00:01:09.472 --> 00:01:11.059
Then ride the park.

00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:15.100
Every teammate presents their section. Twelve teams, one park.
